# visual regression
# CI (linux) baselines ARE committed — they are the source of truth.
# Locally-generated ones are per-developer scratch and must never be pushed,
# or two machines' font rasterisation ends up arguing in the diff.
visual/__screenshots__/*-win32.png
visual/__screenshots__/*-darwin.png
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/

# Jetro's installer writes agent config into the repo for every vendor it knows
# about, and none of it belongs in git.
#
#   .mcp.json, .cursor/mcp.json, .codex/config.toml — absolute paths into one
#   machine's C:\Users\...\.jetro install, plus that machine's whole PATH.
#
#   CLAUDE.md, AGENT.md, .windsurfrules, .cursor/rules/agent.mdc,
#   .agents/rules/agent.md, .github/copilot-instructions.md — six copies of the
#   same 1032-byte "You are an assistant for the Jetro research platform" blurb,
#   which says nothing about XUI. AGENTS.md is this repo's real one.
#
#   .agents/skills/ — a stale mirror of .claude/skills/. Four of the six matched
#   when this was written and two had drifted, which is the whole argument: a
#   duplicate that goes out of date is worse than no duplicate, because an agent
#   reading the stale copy follows superseded instructions and thinks it complied.
.mcp.json
.cursor/
.codex/
.agents/
.windsurfrules
AGENT.md
CLAUDE.md
.github/copilot-instructions.md

# ad-hoc debugging screenshots and the throwaway scripts that take them
screenshot.png
shot-*.png
